{
 "_source": "[4.45a/b/c] Organization at Arrival Charts (scratchpad/port/transcriptions/4.45a-oa-allied.md, 4.45b-oa-italian.md, 4.45c-oa-german.md), mapped onto the campaign OOB counters (oob_italian.json + oob_campaign_extra.json + reinforcements_campaign.json). Keyed by counter string; game.oob._seed_organization resolves parent counters to engine unit ids and sets Unit.assigned_to (19.11, the paper parent) + Unit.org_type (the [19.3] Formation Organization row on an HQ). attached_to is NOT seeded: the VASSAL extraction scatters each formation one unit per hex, so no formation is co-located at setup (19.12 attachment requires the same hex); the tree is the paper structure that makes [15.53] REACHABLE once a formation concentrates and attaches. PROVENANCE: every tree here is transcribed from the OA charts EXCEPT the two flagged reconstructions (62nd Marmarica / 63rd Cirene, see _flags), which are inferred from the counter naming, not charted.",
 "_org_types": "The [19.3] row names live in data/formation_organization.json.",
 "_flags": [
  "SUPERSEDED 2026-07-27 (Phase 8.1c division-HQ pass) for Ariete, Littorio, Folgore and 136 GGFF: each of these four DOES carry an HQ counter printed on its own [4.44b] sheet (Ariete p.147, Littorio p.148, Folgore p.154, 136 GGFF p.154) and it is now seeded (reinforcements_campaign.json) with its melded sub-units re-parented to it. Still true, unresolved, for the OTHER melded Italian reinforcement divisions this flag names -- Trieste, Trento, Bologna, Brescia, Savona, Sabratha, Sirte, Pistoia, Pavia -- which carry no HQ counter in this OOB (2-4 melded counters each) and stay independent, not seedable without inventing a counter the book does not print for them here.",
  "SUPERSEDED 2026-07-27 (Phase 8.1c division-HQ pass) for 2nd Libyan: its Div HQ^E (scan p.148, counter '2 Libyan') is now seeded (oob_campaign_extra.json) and its two infantry regiments (IT 3 Libyan / IT 4 Libyan) re-parented under it -- their own regiment->battalion structure is unchanged, still transcribed. 64th Catanzaro (chart p.153) is UNCHANGED by that pass -- it is not in the 8.1c task's named list -- and still carries no seedable division-HQ counter, so its two infantry regiments stay independent SP-2 Parent Formations exactly as this flag originally described.",
  "JUDGEMENT CALL (not transcribed): 62nd Marmarica and 63rd Cirene appear NOWHERE on the OA chart -- they are named only as the historical attachment destinations of the LXII(L)/LXIII(L) tank battalions (LTC sheet note b, chart p.149). Their two-regiment structure (115+116 / 157+158, each with I/II/III battalions) is RECONSTRUCTED from the oob_campaign_extra.json counter naming plus the universal Italian binary-division pattern -- matching that file's own 'Cirene/Marmarica reconstructed (no [4.44b] sheet)' provenance note, NOT an OA transcription.",
  "4th CCNN battalion 170: the OA puts it under the 270th Legion but counter 'IT 170 - 240-4CN' states the 240th; the counter's stated parent is followed.",
  "Garrisons (Tobruk/Benghazi/Bardia/Derna/minor) and all Unassigned/Corps/Non-Divisional sheets are flat lists of independent units (OA), correctly left with no parent.",
  "LATENT (found by the Gate D honesty audit 2026-07-25, behaviorally INERT here): the CW 1st and 2nd Armoured Divisions' armored regiments (2 Bays/10 Hussars/9 Lancers under 1 Armd Div; the cruiser regts + 2/7 RTR under 2 Armd Div) are parented to the DIVISION HQ, one tier too high -- the [4.45a] scan (PDF p.116) and transcription 4.45a-oa-allied.md:88-91 nest them at L2 under the 2nd Armoured Bde HQ, leaving that brigade HQ childless. Inert in this slice because concentrate_formations attaches only under COMBAT HQs and both the division and brigade HQs are non-combat (neuter==base determinism holds regardless); it becomes a real faithfulness bug only when non-combat HQ-follows-formation movement lands. A correct fix must re-read the whole [4.45a] CW armored chart (p.116-132) to enumerate every armored-brigade regiment and its brigade parent -- a partial fix would leave the tree internally inconsistent; tracked as a CW-armored-OOB follow-up.",
  "The five ENGINEER counters the 8.1b OOB pass added whose formation IS treed are treed here (2026-07-27, review repair): 200 Pioneer Bn [5 Le], 33 Pioneer Bn, 900 Pioneer Bn, 200 Pioneer Bn [164], 2/1 Aus Pioneer Bn. Each is TRANSCRIBED from the OA chart's own assignment notation -- [4.44b]'s key (scan p.147, verbatim): \"A unit whose name is indented two spaces possesses a parent formation. Its parent unit is the first unit above it on the sheet whose name is not indented.\" All five print at that one indent under their division headquarters (5th Light p.162, 15th Panzer p.163, 90th Light p.166, 164th Light p.164, 9th Australian p.125), exactly like the Panzerjaeger/Flak/Aufklarungs battalions already treed beside them. NOT treed, correctly: the eight Italian Engineer Battalions (Trento, Brescia, Sabratha, Pavia, Bologna, Savona, Trieste, Pistoia) -- those divisions are melded counters with no HQ in this OOB, so the WHOLE formation is untreed, not just its engineer (the first flag above); 778 Naval Eng Koy, which the chart itself files under 'Unassigned Infantry Units' (p.164) with no parent; and 288 Pioneer Coy, already treed under 288 Son HQ.",
  "Phase 8.1c division-HQ pass (2026-07-27): seeded the HQ counters the [4.44B]/[4.45b] OA charts print but this OOB never carried -- Ariete, Littorio, Folgore, 1st Libyan, 2nd Libyan, 136 GGFF, RECAM, and the 31st/32nd Gaf S di C (Tobruk) and 30th Gaf S di C (Bardia) on the Axis side; 7th Armoured, 44th Infantry, 6th Australian, 4th Indian and 2nd New Zealand on the Commonwealth side. REPAIRED 2026-07-27 by this pass's own review: (a) the 1st Libyan Div HQ was seeded TWICE. 'IT 1 Libyan - none', already on the map at C4020, IS that HQ -- the [4.44b] sheet's only un-indented row, the module counter art's Eng-flagged 'IT 1 Libyan - none.svg', and [60.31]'s own 'C4020: 1 Libyan Div (I)' all say so -- and this pass had parented it under its own duplicate. The duplicate is deleted and the real counter carries the it_libyan_division org_type (see data/oob_italian.json's _role_comment on that record). So FOURTEEN counters were added, not fifteen. (b) All nine Italian division/garrison HQs are hq_engineer, not hq: the chart prints HQ^E on every one. RECAM alone is a plain HQ and stays one. (c) The 7th Armoured and 4th Indian HQs moved to the hexes [60.41] prints for them (D3612, D3615), and the 6th Australian and 2nd New Zealand HQs moved out of the reinforcement schedule to the at-start hexes [60.41] prints (E1430 Helwan, E3613 Alexandria), their chart Arrives cell being 'D'. All fourteen are role hq/hq_engineer, is_combat False. MEASURED, campaign_policy.concentrate_formations at t0 (both sides, seed 4): ZERO attach orders name any of the fifteen, before or after this pass (16 Axis / 0 Allied orders either way) -- concentrate_formations only attaches under a COMBAT parent (see its own docstring), and every one of these fifteen HQs is non-combat, exactly like every pre-existing German Parent Formation the docstring already names. So this pass is currently INERT for live concentration (org_type on a bare non-combat HQ has no reader until the HQ-follows-its-formation movement this project has not built), and it is not claimed to be more than that: it completes the OOB and the paper tree the book prints, ready for whenever that mechanism lands. 'HQ 44 Inf Div' REPLACES the fabricated '44 Inf Div body' stand-in (no OA-chart basis, is_combat True) with the real, non-combat counter the chart prints. 'RECAM HQ' re-homes the pre-existing 'RECAM Recon Group' reinforcement from the catch-all 'Unassigned Reconnaissance' formation to its own -- same turn and hex, a relabel not a new placement. 31 Guastatori Engineer Bn (RECAM's own chart-printed engineer battalion, ID bbb) has no counter anywhere in this OOB and is left independent, flagged, not fabricated -- there is nothing yet to attach. The 30th/31st Gaf S di C HQs stand with NO sub-battalion at all (their I/II/III battalions are unseeded, a pre-existing extraction gap); 32nd Gaf S di C parents the one battalion this OOB does seed (IT III - 32 GaF).",
  "TWO OF THAT PASS'S PARENT LINKS ARE WITHDRAWN 2026-07-27 by the 8.1c gate-honesty audit, which read the two sheets: both were assignments the OA chart does not print, and this file's own _source promises every tree here is an OA transcription bar the two flagged reconstructions. (1) '3rd Hussars [7]' -> 'HQ 7 Armd Div' is DELETED. The [4.44B] chart files the 3rd Kings Own Hussars under 'Unassigned Armor-Class Units' (scan p.122, counter abbr '3 Hus', ID 'g', Arrives 3/4, each row an independent unit), and its own note a there says the unit was later assigned to the 9th Armored Brigade of the 10th Armored Division -- never to the 7th Armoured. The 7th Armoured sheet (p.117) does not list it. The link rested on the counter string's '[7]', which is an OCR ERROR: [4.43a], the Commonwealth Land Unit Reinforcement and Withdrawal Schedule, prints 'GT 4 OpS 3: 3rd Hussars [T]' -- an italic capital T, read off a 600dpi render for this audit, in the same TYPE bracket the same chart uses for '1st, The Royal Dragoons [R]' and '106 RHA [AT]' and [60.31] uses for 'I(M) [T; Ar/LTC]'. T is Tank, not the 7th Armoured Division. NOT FIXED HERE, FLAGGED: the PRE-EXISTING counter string '3rd Hussars [7]' and its group 'CW 7th Armoured Division' in data/reinforcements_campaign.json carry the same OCR error, as does docs/rules/90-charts-tables-and-play-aids.md's [4.43a] table; renaming a counter changes its engine unit id and is a re-extraction's job, not an audit repair. (2) 'I(L) Carri Bn' -> 'Ariete Div HQ' is DELETED. The Ariete sheet (p.147) prints the I(L) and II(L) Tank Battalions with note e against them, verbatim: 'The two Light Tank battalions are attached, not assigned. They are listed here as they arrived with the Ariete and saw a considerable amount of combat while controlled by the division.' assigned_to IS [19.11] assignment, and this file deliberately seeds no attached_to at all, so the faithful encoding of an ATTACHED-not-assigned battalion is no link. The Ariete's other four seeded sub-units are untouched: 8 Bersaglieri Regt and Ariete Arty print at the two-space (division) indent, and VIII/IX Carri print at the four-space indent whose division-equivalent parent the chart's own key names as the division HQ counter (their brigade tier, 132 Regt Corazzata HQ, has no counter in this OOB -- the same shape as the three 7Spt units under HQ 7 Armd Div). MEASURED, campaign(seed=4), each arm neutered by rewriting THIS FILE (which is what game.oob._load reads, so there is no import binding to miss) and each arm its own process (so the process-reuse neuter trap tests/baselines.py records cannot bite): both links restored 1488074e20bf / 277274 events == the pre-repair tree; I(L) deleted only 1488074e20bf / 277274 -- THE I(L) DELETION MOVES NOTHING; 3rd Hussars deleted only 2adb020c534b / 277273 == live, so the Hussars deletion is the whole move. The two benchmark signatures are UNCHANGED (87f3baeb4530 / b2a2f8bf6ab9 -- only campaign() reads this file) so no re-baseline is owed, the campaign is byte-identical run-to-run at 2adb020c534b, invariants hold across the whole 277,273-event 111-turn fold, and the full suite is 1461 passed / 2 skipped, the same counts as before. THE ONE EVENT THAT DISAPPEARS, NAMED: with the invented link live the war emits exactly one 'CP_EXPENDED / HQ-7-Armd-Div / rebuild' beside the 3rd Hussars' own -- game/engine.py's [19.68] 'one CP per two points, to both' charges the rebuild to unit.assigned_to as well. So the link was not inert bookkeeping: it billed a Command Point to a division the chart never assigns this regiment to."
